<!-- Application Structure Plan: The SPA is redesigned as a complete learning module with a clear, top-down pedagogical structure. It features a sticky navigation bar to access distinct sections: "Beranda" (Home), "Modul 1" (Concepts), "Modul 2" (Features), "Modul 3" (Challenges), "Evaluasi" (Evaluation), and "Referensi" (References). This modular approach was chosen to break down complex information into digestible lessons. User interaction is enhanced with a "next module" button to simulate progress, interactive cards that expand with detailed text, a tabbed interface for comparing features, and an interactive doughnut chart that triggers a modal to provide detailed solutions for each challenge. The new "Evaluasi" section provides a self-assessment quiz with instant feedback and a final score, reinforcing key concepts. The design prioritizes a structured, guided learning path, moving from core concepts to practical application, problem-solving, and finally, self-evaluation. The quiz now has improved interactivity for selecting answers, with visual feedback for selected options before submission and correct/incorrect marking after submission. A new download button is added to allow users to download the module content as a file. -->
<!-- Visualization & Content Choices:
1. Modul 1 (Konsep Dasar): Report Info -> 5 key benefits. Goal -> Inform/Organize. Viz/Method -> Interactive, expandable cards. Interaction -> Clicking a card smoothly expands to reveal a detailed explanation, encouraging users to actively discover information rather than just reading a static list. Justification -> This method is highly effective for self-paced learning, making the content feel less like a report and more like a discovery tool.
2. Modul 2 (Fitur & Fungsionalitas): Report Info -> Table of application types and features. Goal -> Organize/Compare. Viz/Method -> A tabbed interface using HTML buttons and vanilla JS. Interaction -> Clicking a tab button dynamically updates the content area with specific details and features, with a smooth fade effect. Justification -> It prevents information overload and allows students to focus on one category at a time, facilitating comparative learning.
3. Modul 3 (Tantangan & Solusi): Report Info -> List of challenges. Goal -> Inform/Problem-solve. Viz/Method -> A Chart.js doughnut chart. Interaction -> A crucial enhancement: clicking a segment of the chart triggers a JavaScript modal to appear, which provides a detailed explanation of the challenge and actionable solutions. Justification -> This turns a passive visualization into a problem-solving activity, directly engaging students with the material and teaching them how to overcome real-world obstacles.
4. Evaluasi (Self-Assessment): Report Info -> none. Goal -> Assess understanding. Viz/Method -> Interactive multiple-choice quiz with JavaScript validation. Interaction -> Users select answers and click a button to receive a score and feedback. Justification -> A key pedagogical component that allows students to check their comprehension and identify areas for review.
5. Glosarium & Referensi: Report Info -> Key terms and bibliography. Goal -> Provide supplementary information. Viz/Method -> A single, collapsible section. Interaction -> Clicking a button toggles the visibility of the content. Justification -> This keeps the main learning modules clean while ensuring essential academic resources are easily accessible on demand.
All elements are implemented with standard web technologies and the Chart.js library, fully adhering to the NO SVG/Mermaid constraint. -->
